// provenance: ADR-0007 ratification (2026-08-12) — first use of the CANONICAL
// named-regime guard form. Associativity is the poster-child exact-only rule:
// it silently FAILS under floating point, which is what regimes exist to say.
// Raw form `numeric_semantics = exact` remains this guard's declared expansion.
equivalence add_associativity {
    (a + b) + c
    <=>
    a + (b + c)

    guards {
        regime = ExactArithmetic
    }
}
